## 📅 Weekly Cleaning Checklist  

### Monday – Kitchen & Entryway  
- [ ] Clear countertops – Put all dishes in the dishwasher or drying rack; toss any food scraps.  
- [ ] Wipe countertops – Spray all‑purpose cleaner, wipe with a clean microfiber cloth.  
- [ ] Clean sink – Scrub with a non‑abrasive sponge, rinse, and polish with a dry cloth.  
- [ ] Wipe cabinet fronts – Lightly spray and wipe any fingerprints or grease.  
- [ ] Empty trash – Remove bag, tie it, replace with a fresh liner.  
- [ ] Sweep floor – Use a broom or handheld sweeper to collect crumbs and debris.  
- [ ] Mop floor – Fill bucket with warm water + floor cleaner, mop the kitchen and entryway tiles.  
- [ ] Spot‑clean entry mat – Shake out loose dirt, then vacuum or brush the mat surface.  

### Tuesday – Main Bathroom  
- [ ] Apply toilet bowl cleaner – Let sit 5 min, then scrub with toilet brush.  
- [ ] Wipe toilet exterior – Clean seat, lid, tank, and base with disinfectant wipes.  
- [ ] Clean sink & faucet – Spray bathroom cleaner, scrub, rinse, and dry.  
- [ ] Polish mirror – Use glass cleaner and a lint‑free cloth.  
- [ ] Scrub shower walls/tub – Spray shower cleaner, let sit 5 min, scrub with a soft brush, rinse.  
- [ ] Clean showerhead – Soak in white‑vinegar solution (½ cup vinegar in a zip‑bag) for 30 min, then rinse.  
- [ ] Wipe tile grout – Apply a grout‑cleaning paste, scrub lightly, wipe clean.  
- [ ] Replace hand towel – Hang a fresh towel, launder the used one.  

### Wednesday – Living / Common Areas  
- [ ] Dust all surfaces – Shelves, TV stand, coffee table, picture frames, and décor items (use a microfiber duster).  
- [ ] Clean electronics – Lightly mist a cloth with screen cleaner and wipe TV, remote controls, and gaming consoles.  
- [ ] Vacuum carpet/rug – Run the vacuum slowly over high‑traffic zones; go over edges and under lightweight furniture.  
- [ ] Vacuum sofa cushions – Use upholstery attachment; lift cushions to reach underneath.  
- [ ] Fluff and arrange pillows – Rotate decorative pillows for even wear.  
- [ ] Straighten books/magazines – Align spines, place items neatly on shelves or coffee table.  

### Thursday – Bedrooms  
- [ ] Make the bed – Pull up fitted sheet, smooth top sheet, tuck blankets, arrange pillows.  
- [ ] Tidy nightstand – Put away loose items, wipe surface with a damp cloth.  
- [ ] Dust bedside lamps & switches – Use a dry microfiber cloth.  
- [ ] Vacuum or sweep floor – Focus on corners and under the bed.  
- [ ] Change sheets (if scheduled) – Strip the bed, place dirty linens in laundry basket, put on fresh fitted sheet, top sheet, and duvet cover.  
- [ ] Organize a small drawer – Pull out items, discard trash, fold clothing, replace neatly.  

### Friday – Laundry & Linens  
- [ ] Sort laundry – Separate whites, colors, and delicates into three piles.  
- [ ] Start washing machine – Load first pile, add detergent, select appropriate cycle.  
- [ ] Transfer to dryer or hang – Move washed items promptly to avoid mildew.  
- [ ] Fold dried clothes – Fold shirts, pants, towels, and place them in their proper drawers/closets.  
- [ ] Wipe washing machine door seal – Remove residue with a damp cloth.  
- [ ] Clean lint trap – Remove lint from dryer filter (if you have a dryer).  

### Saturday – Rotating Deep‑Clean Spot *(pick ONE each week)*  

| Option | Detailed Steps |
|--------|----------------|
| **Oven & Stovetop** | 1️⃣ Remove oven racks; soak in hot, soapy water. 2️⃣ Spray interior with oven cleaner; let sit 15 min. 3️⃣ Scrub interior with non‑scratch pad, wipe clean. 4️⃣ Clean stovetop burners/grates; wipe spillovers. 5️⃣ Replace racks, wipe exterior. |
| **Refrigerator** | 1️⃣ Take out all food; discard expired items. 2️⃣ Remove shelves/drawers; wash in sink. 3️⃣ Wipe interior walls with a mixture of water + baking soda. 4️⃣ Dry, replace shelves, and restock food. 5️⃣ Clean door seals with a toothbrush and mild soap. |
| **Windows (inside)** | 1️⃣ Spray glass cleaner on window pane. 2️⃣ Wipe with a lint‑free cloth in a “Z” motion. 3️⃣ Clean window sills with a damp cloth. 4️⃣ Dust blinds or curtains. |
| **Baseboards & Door Frames** | 1️⃣ Dust with a dry cloth. 2️⃣ Spot‑clean stains using a damp cloth + mild detergent. 3️⃣ Dry thoroughly to prevent moisture damage. |
| **Closet Declutter** | 1️⃣ Pull everything out onto the floor. 2️⃣ Sort into Keep, Donate, Trash piles. 3️⃣ Vacuum/clean closet floor. 4️⃣ Return kept items, arranging by category. 5️⃣ Place donation box near the door for later drop‑off. |

*(Mark the chosen option with an “X” in the box next to it.)*  

### Sunday – Light Reset & Planning  
- [ ] 5‑minute room reset – Walk through each room, pick up stray items, straighten cushions, close doors.  
- [ ] Sweep/vacuum entryway – Quick brush‑up of the front hall floor.  
- [ ] Check supplies – Note any empty cleaners, trash bags, or paper goods; add to shopping list.  
- [ ] Review upcoming week – Look at appointments, guests, or special cleaning needs; adjust the Saturday deep‑clean slot if necessary.  
- [ ] Set a weekly goal – e.g., “Donate 5 kg of clothes,” “Organize pantry,” etc.  
